      "solution": "h = input().strip()\nr = int(h[0:2], 16)\ng = int(h[2:4], 16)\nb = int(h[4:6], 16)\nlum = 0.299 * r + 0.587 * g + 0.114 * b\nprint(\"LIGHT\" if lum >= 128 else \"DARK\")\n",
      "statement": "Given a 6-character hexadecimal color string [[hexCode]], determine if it is light or dark.\n\nConvert the color into its Red, Green, and Blue decimal components (each between {{0}} and {{255}}):\n- [[R]]: characters 1-2\n- [[G]]: characters 3-4\n- [[B]]: characters 5-6\n\nCalculate perceived luminance [[L]]:\n[[L]] = {{0.299}} * [[R]] + {{0.587}} * [[G]] + {{0.114}} * [[B]]\n\nIf [[L]] ≥ {{128}}, output `LIGHT`.\nOtherwise, output `DARK`.",
